 "response": "Stedamu's budget is now **$2840K**. Only Finance Office budget entries count; all other messages, and Finance notices that don't change the budget, are ignored.\n\n**Method**\n1. I listed every Finance Office withdrawal and followed each chain to the end. If the last withdrawal in a chain is in force, the update before it is cancelled, and so on back down the chain. For example:\n   - #0632 withdraws #0439, which brings back #0112. #0112 withdraws #0078, which brings back #0007. #0007 withdraws #0003, which brings back #0002. So the $36K decrease in #0002 stands.\n   - #1367 cancels #0845, which brings back #0175. #0175 cancels #0057, which brings back #0013. So #0013 withdraws #0010, and the $407K decrease in #0010 does not count.\n2. After resolving all chains, 103 budget updates end up withdrawn. These include #0010, #0015, #0016, #0017, #0022, #0026, #0032, #0037, #0039, #0047, #0062, #0070 and others through #1356.\n3. I started from the $1880K set in #0001 and applied every remaining increase and decrease in record order.\n\n**Selected points along the way**\n\n| After record | Budget |\n|---|---|\n| #0006 | $1282K |\n| #0129 | $4220K |\n| #0300 | $1515K |\n| #0600 | $2062K |\n| #0900 | $2627K |\n| #1200 | $3191K |\n| #1500 | $1695K |\n| #1598 (last budget update) | $2840K |\n\nThis is a long hand calculation, so a small arithmetic slip is possible.\n\nANSWER: $2840K",
